@startuml Git Hooks Detailed Sequence
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 150

title Git Hooks - Detailed Sequence Diagram

actor Developer
participant "Git CLI" as Git
participant "pre-commit\nHook" as PreCommit
participant "Git\nRepository" as Repo
participant "post-commit\nHook" as PostCommit
participant "git status" as GitStatus
participant "sync-ai-use-cases.sh" as SyncScript
database "Use Case Hub" as Hub
participant "Claude Code\nSession" as Claude
participant "SessionEnd\nHook" as SessionEnd
database ".usecase/session-stats/\nYYYY-MM-DD-HHMMSS.txt" as Stats

== Scenario 1: Successful Commit on Feature Branch ==

Developer -> Git: git commit -m "Add new feature"
activate Git

Git -> Git: Check for pre-commit hook
Git -> PreCommit: Execute .git/hooks/pre-commit
activate PreCommit

PreCommit -> PreCommit: Get current branch name\n(git symbolic-ref --short HEAD)
PreCommit -> PreCommit: Check if branch is "main" or "master"

alt Branch is main or master
  PreCommit -> PreCommit: ❌ Branch protection triggered
  PreCommit --> Git: Exit code 1 (FAIL)
  Git --> Developer: ❌ ERROR: Direct commits to protected branches not allowed\n\n**Suggested branch names:**\n  • feature/description\n  • fix/description\n  • docs/description\n  • refactor/description\n  • test/description\n\n**Bypass:** git commit --no-verify
  deactivate PreCommit

else Branch is feature/fix/docs/etc
  PreCommit -> PreCommit: ✓ Branch validation passed
  PreCommit --> Git: Exit code 0 (SUCCESS)
  deactivate PreCommit

  Git -> Repo: Create commit object
  activate Repo
  Repo -> Repo: Update HEAD reference
  Repo -> Repo: Update branch pointer
  Repo --> Git: Commit created (SHA: abc123)
  deactivate Repo

  Git -> Git: Check for post-commit hook
  Git -> PostCommit: Execute .git/hooks/post-commit
  activate PostCommit

  PostCommit -> GitStatus: git diff-tree --no-commit-id\n--name-only -r HEAD
  activate GitStatus
  GitStatus --> PostCommit: List of changed files:\n  • src/feature.js\n  • .usecase/cases/feature-123.md\n  • tests/feature.test.js
  deactivate GitStatus

  PostCommit -> PostCommit: Check if any .md files in\n.usecase/cases/ were modified

  alt .usecase/cases/ files changed
    PostCommit -> PostCommit: ✓ AI use case changes detected
    PostCommit -> PostCommit: Resolve sync script path:\n1. Check $AI_USECASES_SYNC_SCRIPT\n2. Check $AI_USECASES_DIR\n3. Default: ~/Documents/ai-use-case-hub/\n   sync-ai-use-cases.sh

    PostCommit -> SyncScript: Execute sync script
    activate SyncScript
    note right of SyncScript
      Sync script performs:
      1. Copy .usecase/ to hub
      2. Create symlinks
      3. git add & commit
      4. git push to remote
    end note

    SyncScript -> Hub: Copy documentation files
    activate Hub
    Hub --> SyncScript: Files copied

    SyncScript -> Hub: Create symlinks\nfor organization
    Hub --> SyncScript: Symlinks created

    SyncScript -> Hub: git add .
    SyncScript -> Hub: git commit -m "Sync from project"
    Hub --> SyncScript: Commit created

    SyncScript -> Hub: git push origin main
    Hub --> SyncScript: Push successful
    deactivate Hub

    SyncScript --> PostCommit: Exit code 0 (SUCCESS)\n✓ Documentation synced
    deactivate SyncScript

    PostCommit --> Git: ✓ Auto-sync completed

  else No .usecase/cases/ changes
    PostCommit -> PostCommit: No AI use case changes
    PostCommit --> Git: No sync needed
  end

  deactivate PostCommit

  Git --> Developer: ✓ Commit successful: abc123\n[feature/new-feature abc123] Add new feature\n 3 files changed, 42 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)
end

deactivate Git

== Scenario 2: Commit to Protected Branch (Blocked) ==

Developer -> Git: git commit -m "Fix bug"
activate Git
note right of Developer: Currently on main branch
Git -> PreCommit: Execute .git/hooks/pre-commit
activate PreCommit

PreCommit -> PreCommit: Get current branch: "main"
PreCommit -> PreCommit: ❌ Protected branch detected

PreCommit --> Git: Exit code 1 (FAIL)
deactivate PreCommit

Git --> Developer: ❌ ERROR: Cannot commit to main\n\n╔═══════════════════════════════════════╗\n║  COMMIT TO PROTECTED BRANCH BLOCKED   ║\n╚═══════════════════════════════════════╝\n\nYou are currently on branch: main\n\nDirect commits to 'main' and 'master'\nbranches are not allowed.\n\nPlease create a feature branch instead.\n\n**Bypass (not recommended):**\ngit commit --no-verify
deactivate Git

== Scenario 3: Post-Commit Hook with Sync Failure (Non-Blocking) ==

Developer -> Git: git commit -m "Update docs"
activate Git
note right of Developer: On feature/docs-update branch

Git -> PreCommit: Execute pre-commit hook
activate PreCommit
PreCommit -> PreCommit: ✓ Branch validation passed
PreCommit --> Git: Exit code 0
deactivate PreCommit

Git -> Repo: Create commit
activate Repo
Repo --> Git: Commit created
deactivate Repo

Git -> PostCommit: Execute post-commit hook
activate PostCommit

PostCommit -> GitStatus: Get changed files
activate GitStatus
GitStatus --> PostCommit: .usecase/cases/docs-update.md
deactivate GitStatus

PostCommit -> PostCommit: ✓ Use case changes detected
PostCommit -> SyncScript: Execute sync script
activate SyncScript

SyncScript -> Hub: Attempt to sync
activate Hub
Hub --> SyncScript: ❌ ERROR: Hub repository not found\nor network issue
deactivate Hub

SyncScript --> PostCommit: Exit code 1 (FAILURE)
deactivate SyncScript

PostCommit -> PostCommit: Log warning (non-fatal)
PostCommit --> Git: ⚠ Warning: Sync failed\n(commit still successful)
deactivate PostCommit

Git --> Developer: ✓ Commit successful\n⚠ Warning: Could not sync to hub\nManually run: ai-use-case sync
deactivate Git

== Scenario 4: Claude Code Session End ==

Developer -> Claude: End session (/exit or close)
activate Claude

Claude -> Claude: Prepare session end cleanup
Claude -> Claude: Check for .claude/hooks/SessionEnd

Claude -> SessionEnd: Execute SessionEnd hook
activate SessionEnd

SessionEnd -> SessionEnd: Capture session metadata:\n• Timestamp: 2025-12-08 23:30:45\n• Repository path\n• Current branch

SessionEnd -> SessionEnd: git log --since="2 hours ago"\n--pretty=format:"  %h - %s (%ar)"
note right of SessionEnd
  Captures recent commits
  from last 2 hours to
  correlate with session
end note

SessionEnd -> SessionEnd: git status --short
note right of SessionEnd
  Checks for uncommitted
  changes made during
  the session
end note

SessionEnd -> SessionEnd: Create statistics file:\n.usecase/session-stats/\n2025-12-08-233045.txt

SessionEnd -> Stats: Write session data
activate Stats
note right of Stats
  **File Contents:**
  ================
  Session End: 2025-12-08 23:30:45
  Repository: ai-use-case-cli
  Branch: feature/new-feature

  Recent Commits (last 2h):
  - abc123 Add new feature
  - def456 Update tests

  Uncommitted Changes: Yes
  - Modified: src/feature.js
  - Modified: tests/feature.test.js

  Run /cost for full statistics
  ================
end note
Stats --> SessionEnd: File created
deactivate Stats

SessionEnd --> Claude: Exit code 0\n✓ Session statistics saved
deactivate SessionEnd

Claude --> Developer: ✓ Session ended\nStatistics saved to:\n.usecase/session-stats/2025-12-08-233045.txt
deactivate Claude

== Scenario 5: Bypass Pre-Commit Hook (Emergency) ==

Developer -> Git: git commit -m "Hotfix" --no-verify
activate Git
note right of Developer: Using --no-verify flag\nto bypass hooks

Git -> Git: Check --no-verify flag
Git -> Git: ✓ Skip pre-commit hook

Git -> Repo: Create commit directly
activate Repo
Repo --> Git: Commit created on main
deactivate Repo

Git -> Git: Skip post-commit hook\n(due to --no-verify)

Git --> Developer: ✓ Commit successful (hooks bypassed)\n⚠ Warning: Pre-commit protections were skipped
deactivate Git

note right of Developer
  **Use --no-verify sparingly!**
  Only for emergencies or
  when hooks are causing issues
end note

@enduml
